   "analysis": "`_getitem_lowerdim` loops over the tuple in reverse order (the GH60600 change). For `df.loc[row, [cols]]` it first selects the column list, which builds a full temporary column-subset frame. It then calls `section.loc[row]`, which goes through `fast_xs` and returns a view into that temporary 2D block. The small Series keeps the big temporary array alive. The fix most likely belongs here: select the row first when the row key is a scalar, or copy the result. A change in `BlockManager.fast_xs` is also possible.",
